-- title:
--   Chart functions lie in the Gauss prolongation, with explicit residues
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ and $M\neq 0$ with $p\mid M$ and $M/p\neq 0$, a subgroup $H\le(\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times$, and assume the $q$-series $j(q)$ (`jqModC ℚ`) lies in the field $\mathbb{Q}$-generated by the integral form ratios for $\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$, so that the element $j$ of the full level function field is available. Let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ whose residue field is algebraically closed of characteristic $p$, let $\rho\colon \mathrm{R}\,p\to A$ be a ring map with $A\hookrightarrow\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ after $\rho$ equal to the structure map $\mathrm{R}\,p\to\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, and let the $\mathrm{R}\,p$-algebra structure on $A$ be given by $\rho$. Let $\gamma$ be a ring homomorphism from $A\otimes_{\mathrm{R}\,p}T$, where $T$ is the $j$-finite chart algebra (elements of the level-$\Gamma_M(H)$ $q$-expansion function field over $\mathbb{Q}$ integral over $\mathrm{R}\,p[j]$), to the intermediate field `xHFunctionFieldBar M H` of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}((q))$, and assume on pure tensors that the Laurent series of $\gamma(a\otimes b)$ is $a$ times the coefficientwise image in $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}((q))$ of the $q$-expansion of $b$. Let $Rg$ be a regular prolongation of $A$ to that field with residue field `JHNeronObjectAtP.Fbar p M H hpM` of the residue field of $A$, i.e. a valuation subring $Rg.\mathrm{integers}$ together with a surjective residue map with kernel the maximal ideal, inducing on $A$ the residue map of $A$, and contracting to $A$ along $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$. Assume the Gauss description: $f\in Rg.\mathrm{integers}$ iff there are Laurent series $x,y$ over $A$ with the coefficientwise reduction of $y$ nonzero and $f\cdot y=x$ coefficientwise in $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}((q))$; and assume that any Laurent series $y$ over $A$ whose image lies in the field belongs to $Rg.\mathrm{integers}$ with residue the coefficientwise reduction of $y$. Then (i) $\gamma$ maps the whole tensor product into $Rg.\mathrm{integers}$, and (ii) for all $a\in A$, $b\in T$ and every Laurent series $y$ over $\mathrm{R}\,p$ whose coefficientwise image in $\mathbb{Q}((q))$ is the $q$-expansion of $b$, the element $\gamma(a\otimes b)$ lies in $Rg.\mathrm{integers}$ and its residue, read as a Laurent series over the residue field of $A$, equals $\bar a$ times the coefficientwise reduction of $y$ along $\rho$.
--
--   This identifies the composite of $\gamma$ with the Gauss residue map as coefficientwise reduction of integral $q$-expansions, so that the $j$-finite chart of the Deligne–Rapoport model over $A$ lands in the Gauss valuation ring at the cusp and its reduction is the $q$-expansion of the corresponding function on the component at infinity. It is used in the branch analysis of the two-chart integral model at a crossing prime, by [`ModularCurve.XHDRModelAtP.exists_branch_primes_gauss_iff_and_hasValue_of_crossing_prime`](thm.html#ModularCurve.XHDRModelAtP.exists_branch_primes_gauss_iff_and_hasValue_of_crossing_prime), [`ModularCurve.XHDRModelAtP.exists_snd_branch_prime_of_crossing_prime_of_regularProlongation`](thm.html#ModularCurve.XHDRModelAtP.exists_snd_branch_prime_of_crossing_prime_of_regularProlongation) and [`ModularCurve.XHDRModelAtP.hasValue_placeOn0_and_placeOn1_of_mul_eq_of_not_mem_crossing_prime`](thm.html#ModularCurve.XHDRModelAtP.hasValue_placeOn0_and_placeOn1_of_mul_eq_of_not_mem_crossing_prime).
